    <title>Problems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>Problem</th><th>Clinical status</th><th>Verification</th><th>Code</th><th>Provenance</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  <tr ID="problem-1">
    <td>Numbness, tingling and loss of position sense in the fingers of both hands for three weeks, worse on the left, with clumsiness that makes her lose her place on the fingerboard, an electric feeling down the spine on bending the neck (Lhermitte&apos;s sign), and fatigue; a similar month of tingling in the fingers 18 months ago settled on its own. A lesion of the cervical spinal cord must be found: MRI of the brain and spine with contrast booked this week</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>R20.2</td><td>S — Synthetic presenting problem anchored to her documented loss of sensation in her fingers and fatigue. Superseded by the diagnosis at the second visit.</td>
  </tr></tbody></table></text>

